    "final_message": "The red acceptance test is written and committed as e54393e. `scripts/verify story-drafting` passes tessercheck, `mypy --strict` and the non-root tests. Its root-tier pytest step fails at the user story's *then*, which is the intended red.\n\n**Test:** `TestSubmittingAJtbd::test_a_just_submitted_jtbd_is_drafting`, in `story-drafting/tests/test_acceptance.py`.\n\n**What it does:**\n- It posts a JTBD to `/jtbds` on the served host and gets a 201.\n- It retries `GET /jtbds/{jtbd_id}` until that answers 200.\n- It then asserts `check_jtbd.get(\"step\") == \"drafting\"`.\n\n**Failure:**\n```\nassert (submit_jtbd_status, check_jtbd_status) == (201, 200)   # passes\n> assert check_jtbd.get(\"step\") == \"drafting\"\nE AssertionError: assert None == 'drafting'\n```\nThe read answers only `jtbd_id`, `situation`, `motivation` and `outcome`, so it has no `step`. The log shows 1 failed.\n\n**Spec** (`<repo>/.baseline-runs/red-v9-sonnet-medium/spec.toml`):\n- **App and context:** `story_drafting`, bounded context `drafting`, aggregate `Jtbd`, identity `jtbd_id`, storage `memory`, host `http`.\n- **Fields:** the aggregate has three `str` fields taken from the JTBD's when/want/so-can: `situation`, `motivation`, `outcome`.\n- **Operations:**\n  - client write is `submit_jtbd`, client read is `check_jtbd`\n  - orchestrator is `draft_stories` in `start` calling mode, since the workflow will wait on a person\n  - action is `write_drafts`\n  - repository is `save_jtbd` / `load_jtbd`, collection `jtbds`\n\n**Decisions:**\n- **Aggregate has no status field.** This keeps the behavior out of the tree, so the read cannot answer \"drafting\" yet.\n- **`step` is my name for the read's field.** I picked it from the README's \"the step it is at\". It has no counterpart in the spec.\n- **Test name diverges from the spec.** I renamed only the method, from the spec's `test_a_submitted_jtbd_is_drafting` to `test_a_just_submitted_jtbd_is_drafting`. The class name is unchanged."
  },
